    description: "After PR 5 (WI-kosug; owner ruling 2026-11-20 \"keep as built\"), Rust `#[cfg]` guards and Swift `#if`/`#elseif`/`#else` branches enter the stable id at every level of the scope chain. Three gaps remain:\n\n1. C and C++ `#ifdef`/`#if` alternatives still tie. Repro in kosug/other_languages: `open_file` x2, `struct S` x2, `K::run` x2. No ruling covers C/C++.\n2. Rust inner `#![cfg(...)]` and `cfg_attr(..., cfg(...))` are not read.\n3. Predicates are hashed as written, neither reordered nor evaluated, so `any(a, b)` and `any(b, a)` hash apart.\n\nEach fix moves ids and needs a scheme bump.\n\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/kosug/RESULTS.md."  # b936
